WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.382
Back at Dot's, Panther and Jane were not speaking to each other.

2
00:00:06.383 --> 00:00:11.963
"This is a very pretty dress," said Dot, the owner of the shop.

3
00:00:11.964 --> 00:00:14.678
"Thank you. It's exactly what I wanted,"

4
00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:18.890
Panther replied, but she was glaring at Jane.

5
00:00:18.892 --> 00:00:24.552
"I think it makes you look fat," Jane said in a mean voice.

6
00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:27.823
"You girls should be nice to each other.

7
00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:31.017
Aren't you sisters?" Dot asked.

8
00:00:31.018 --> 00:00:34.485
But neither Panther nor Jane replied.

9
00:00:34.486 --> 00:00:40.733
Meanwhile at the game store, Cy was ready to pay for his purchases.

10
00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:50.108
"Your total comes to one thousand fifty-six dollars and seventy-one cents," the clerk said wearily.

11
00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:58.205
Cy paused. "Uh, how much is that in gold coins?" he asked.

12
00:00:58.206 --> 00:01:03.808
"Excuse me? Did you say gold coins?" asked the clerk.

13
00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:06.200
"Yes. That's what I have here."

14
00:01:06.201 --> 00:01:08.727
Cy pointed to his bag.

15
00:01:08.728 --> 00:01:12.879
"Half of it's mine," Bobby said angrily.

16
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:22.450
"I'm sorry," the clerk said, "but we only accept cash, credit card, or check."

17
00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:24.929
"But these are worth a lot of money,"

18
00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:29.742
Cy pleaded as he held out a coin.

19
00:01:29.743 --> 00:01:31.919
"It looks like play money,"

20
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.658
the clerk said, taking the gold coin from him.

21
00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:37.740
"They're real, I tell you,"

22
00:01:37.741 --> 00:01:42.215
argued Cy, but the clerk did not believe him.

23
00:01:42.216 --> 00:01:44.672
Jane felt like crying.

24
00:01:44.673 --> 00:01:48.616
"It's not fair," she thought to herself.

25
00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:52.917
"Why does Panther get to do whatever she wants?

26
00:01:52.918 --> 00:01:56.971
I have money too."

27
00:01:56.972 --> 00:02:02.532
"That'll be twenty-one dollars and sixty cents," smiled Dot.

28
00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:05.645
"Fine," Panther replied.

29
00:02:05.646 --> 00:02:11.855
She began counting out some gold coins.

30
00:02:11.856 --> 00:02:17.416
"Sweetie, we don't accept foreign currency here," Dot said.

31
00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:21.756
"These aren't foreign," laughed Panther.

32
00:02:21.757 --> 00:02:24.625
"These are gold coins."

33
00:02:24.626 --> 00:02:28.270
Dot picked one up suspiciously.

34
00:02:28.271 --> 00:02:32.651
"Where did you get these?" she asked.

35
00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:36.492
Panther glanced over at Jane before answering.

36
00:02:36.493 --> 00:02:38.239
"From my uncle.

37
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.788
He gave them to us as a gift," Panther lied.

38
00:02:42.789 --> 00:02:47.713
Dot narrowed her eyes and stared at Panther.

39
00:02:47.714 --> 00:02:49.711
"Stay right here.

40
00:02:49.712 --> 00:02:53.717
I'm going to make a phone call," she said.

41
00:02:53.718 --> 00:02:57.824
Then Dot disappeared into the back of the store.

42
00:02:57.825 --> 00:03:01.612
Panther grabbed Jane's arm and whispered frantically,

43
00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:05.385
"Jane! I think she's going to call the police!"

44
00:03:05.387 --> 00:03:09.823
Jane crossed her arms and replied, "I don't care.

45
00:03:09.824 --> 00:03:12.973
You're the one in trouble, not me.

46
00:03:12.974 --> 00:03:15.074
I didn't buy the dress."

47
00:03:15.075 --> 00:03:20.639
The situation at the game store wasn't looking any better.

48
00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.942
"Come on, man." Cy continued to argue with the clerk.

49
00:03:25.943 --> 00:03:29.495
"Look, I'll give you all the gold here.

50
00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:33.942
That's going to be worth more than five thousand dollars!"

51
00:03:33.943 --> 00:03:37.499
"That's not fair!" shouted Bobby.

52
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.694
"Some of that is my money!

53
00:03:39.695 --> 00:03:42.666
And I'm going to buy a car!"

54
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:45.376
Bobby grabbed the bag.

55
00:03:45.377 --> 00:03:49.121
"Let go, you little punk!" yelled Cy.

56
00:03:49.122 --> 00:03:53.182
The boys began pulling and tugging at the bag.

57
00:03:53.183 --> 00:04:01.610
Then, like a watermelon splitting open, the bag ripped in two, and the gold coins flew out everywhere.

58
00:04:01.611 --> 00:04:05.515
At Dot's, Panther had to make a quick decision.

59
00:04:05.516 --> 00:04:09.440
"Jane, we have to get out of here," she said.

60
00:04:09.441 --> 00:04:17.767
When Jane didn't respond, Panther grabbed her arm and dragged her out of the store.

61
00:04:17.768 --> 00:04:23.206
"Get back here, girls!" Dot shouted, running toward them.

62
00:04:23.207 --> 00:04:25.447
"I said, come back!"

63
00:04:25.448 --> 00:04:33.108
Without a backward glance, Panther and Jane ran off as fast as they could.

64
00:04:33.109 --> 00:04:37.619
The clerk at the game store was very angry now.

65
00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.870
"I'm going to call the cops," he threatened.

66
00:04:41.871 --> 00:04:46.357
"For what?" Cy asked in a shaky voice.

67
00:04:46.358 --> 00:04:50.988
"For trying to use counterfeit money," the clerk replied.

68
00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:52.406
"But this is real.

69
00:04:52.407 --> 00:04:54.408
It's real gold, I tell you!"

70
00:04:54.409 --> 00:04:59.833
Cy argued, but it was all in vain.

